A||N||9||jlruiz67||exhaust manifold installation ??||||5||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||01-26-2001||03:27 PM||||Has anyone installed the front exhaust manifold (closer to the firewall) without droping the engine? I'm as always short on cash and the front exhaust manifold just decided to develope a big crack and you cant stand the noise. How long can I drive my car in this condition? what will happen if I keep driving my fiero with this big crack on the exhaust manifold? Any info will help. <P>Thank you all||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||01-26-2001||03:34 PM||||Ive replaced my on my 87 GT..I wont sugar coat it, <B>ITS NO FUN!!!!!</B><BR>I didnt drop the engine, what I did was remove the decklid (<B><I>very</B></I> easy to do, and WELL worth it), then set a pad (I used a shooter's pad) over the engine, got up on it, and went to work. It is a serious, let me say that again, SERIOUS pain in the a$$. Ive heard some people say that it wasnt that difficult....<I>hmmm</I>...ok.<BR>At any rate, I finally got it finished. The main problem was the bolt on the far right side on the bottom side of the manifold...EEK!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <BR>As far as causing probs, that I dont know. I changed mine as soon as I noticed it had a leak...sounded like a helicopter! <BR>Anyway, its not fun, but can be done!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>OH! I almost forgot, take care not to break any rusty bolts!!! Then you'd REALLY have a headache!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000002||jlruiz67||01-26-2001||04:02 PM||||Do you think that wrapping or patching the area on a temporary basis would harm anything, I might need some time to get the parts and time to do the job and this is my only car. Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-26-2001||04:04 PM||||it can cause you to burn a valve. far as I know you have to drop the front of cradle. also makes engine cmpt run a lot hotter, which Fieros dont need. also if you get out the studs without them breaking buy a set of new ones, either stainless or grade 8. the factory ones are grade 4 i think. also use some anti sieze compound to help if you ever have to take them out again.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||01-26-2001||04:16 PM||||You can do a search on this subject....there's a ton of information on manifold replacement and repair.<P>What I did was to first remove the exhaust system... everything from the joint between the cat and wye pipe on back.  This provided much more room to work from the bottom.  The AC compressor also had to be moved out of the way(but NOT disconnected) to gain access to the manifold bolts for cylinder #2.<P>Not a fun job. Fortunately, none of my manifold studs/bolts were seized.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||01-26-2001||05:06 PM||||I did mine from underneath with the car on jackstands. The biggest pain was one bolt behind the AC compressor (I think this would be a problem from any direction). I wound up taking the AC compressor loose and letting it hang to get clearance. Also, take 5 minutes or so to remove the big heat shield on the firewall. It only gives another inch or two clearance, but it really helps.<P>One other note... mine has a replacement catalytic convertor which is much smaller than the factory one, so I could reach around it. With the factory one you may have to drop the exhaust.<P>Like My7Fieros said... it's no fun. At least from underneath you are lying comfortably on your back though...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula 18||01-26-2001||05:34 PM||||I just did mine and i wasn't that bad at all. I jacked up the car and removed the whole exhaust system then went to work on the bolts. You can reach up in between the firewall and the motor from the bottom. I don't have AC so there wasn't much in the way. Now I just have to get the rust off them and weld the feet so I can post them. <P>Good Luck. <BR>Brain ||||reg||1
Z||000007||jlruiz67||01-26-2001||07:32 PM||||what do you guys think, I can buy a set of 85 v6 exhaust manifolds for 100.00 in good working order. Good price for the set?<BR>I will have to put them in myself but the price seems good to me||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||01-27-2001||12:30 PM||||sounds like good deal if there ok. I paid dealer $130 each for new.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bruce||01-27-2001||07:30 PM||||I lucked out: I paid $70 for a ported pair through the Mall.||||reg||1
